{
 "$comment": "The server's Python image (Modal), shared by src/lib/server/modal.ts and scripts/modal-image.mjs (prebuilds it). Top-level pins, resolved together for CPython 3.12 on x86_64 Linux (uv pip compile, 2026-11-18). Change a pin: re-resolve, then run npm run modal:image so the first run after a deploy doesn't build it. `installed` is every distribution the resolution brings in (normalized names): the server installs a cell's other imports from PyPI automatically. `system`: a layer after the packages (so changing it doesn't reinstall them): ffmpeg, for animations as MP4 video, and the server's animation limits. `datasets`: a layer keeping datasets whose own host is slow (CIFAR: 170 MB at 400 kB/s) in the image: torchvision's files under /opt/bj-datasets/<host>/<path> (bj_capture's download_url hook copies them), Keras's in its own cache. `|| true`: a download failing at build time must not fail the image.",
